 "notes": "All official intervals come from one document family: the Tesla Model 3 Owner's Manual in several editions and languages, plus the Tesla DIY page. They are NOT independent of each other. The only independent sources are Zecar (AU) and Everyday Chris, and that blog explicitly restates Tesla. No source read gives a scheduled interval for reduction-gear/drive-unit oil, HV inspection, periodic service or battery coolant, and the manual says battery coolant is not replaced for the life of the vehicle under most circumstances. Zecar lists 'Drive unit coolant replacement' but gives no interval. No source distinguishes RWD, Long Range or Performance. The Israeli editions (en_il, he_il) match the US/EU wording, except that tire rotation is stated in km only. The key open decision is which edition governs brake fluid: every 2 years in the as-delivered 2021-2022 editions, every 4 years in the 2024+ editions. tesla.com blocked direct fetches (403), so official quotes come from Wayback captures, with timestamps in the URLs."
}